Don’t let the producers block—use a non‑blocking `select` (or a buffered channel big enough) and close it only after all producers finish.

```go
var wg sync.WaitGroup
for _, p := range producers {
    wg.Add(1)
    go func(p func() int) {
        defer wg.Done()
        for v := range p() {
            select {
            case ch <- v: // send
            default:      // drop if full, avoid deadlock
            }
        }
    }(p)
}
go func() { wg.Wait(); close(ch) }() // close when all done
